{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:labor:audit","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:e74e3b08c58dadb88ede22eb1a84c60923251fc75953ca76915ebdd453bac3a6","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"quantiles","quantiles":[{"probability":0.1,"value":0.9},{"probability":0.5,"value":1.9},{"probability":0.9,"value":3}]},"questionHash":"sha256:20d8e05d3bea415eb4452ff8b599c74a3c3ce1a1b0c2ce11dda57a4e19490197","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq4","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"RESOLVING SERIES AND ITS TRAPS. \"10y nominal benchmark minus 10y inflation swap / TIPS breakeven,\" GDP-weighted across G7, averaged 2032-36. Four construction artefacts, each >3pp:\n\n(1) SWAP-vs-BREAKEVEN IS AN \"OR\". US 10y zero-coupon inflation swaps quote ~15-25bp ABOVE the TIPS-derived breakeven (TIPS carry a liquidity discount). Choosing swaps therefore LOWERS the measured real yield by 15-25bp for the dominant weight. Note also that for the US, nominal minus TIPS breakeven is identically the TIPS real yield (DFII10, the 2.60% anchor in 2A), so the US leg is self-consistent; the \"or\" only bites via the swap option.\n(2) UK RPI->CPIH ALIGNMENT, FEB 2030 — INSIDE THE WINDOW. Index-linked gilts are RPI-linked and RPI breakevens embed the ~80-100bp RPI/CPI wedge. When RPI is aligned to CPIH in Feb 2030, UK breakevens drop mechanically and the UK's measured nominal-minus-breakeven real yield RISES by ~80-100bp with no change in economics. At a ~7% PPP-GDP weight that is +6 to +7bp on the aggregate, arriving as a step mid-window. Direction: UP.\n(3) COVERAGE GAPS. Canada stopped issuing Real Return Bonds in 2022, so a ~5% weight has no forward-looking domestic breakeven market and must be proxied. Japan's 10y inflation swap market is thin and the JGBi market shallow: a low thin-market breakeven (~1.2%) against a normalising 10y JGB (~2.0-2.5%) prints Japan at +0.8 to +1.3% real, versus +0.2 to +0.5% against survey-consistent expectations — ±5 to 10bp on the aggregate. Italy's BTP€i reference is euro-area HICP ex-tobacco, not Italian CPI, which OVERSTATES the Italian real yield whenever Italian inflation exceeds the euro-area average.\n(4) WEIGHT BASIS. PPP GDP weights (per the Section lock) put Japan ~12% and Italy ~6% versus ~8% and ~4% at market rates, i.e. PPP weighting LOWERS the aggregate by ~10-15bp relative to a market-rate construction.\n\nFERMI, 2032-36 averages: US 2.4 (w .44), Japan 0.9 (.12), Germany 1.3 (.10), France 1.6 (.07), UK 2.2 post-alignment (.07), Italy 2.1 (.06), Canada 1.9 (.05) = 1.056+0.108+0.130+0.112+0.154+0.126+0.095 = 1.78 -> P50 1.9, reconciling with the 2.60% US TIPS anchor in 2A minus the non-US drag. P10 0.9 (demand-shortfall/BIS labour-income deficit plus post-bust excess capacity plus explicit repression — note repression typically arrives as nominal yield caps, which on this measure shows up as a LOW real yield only if breakevens do not blow out; if they do, the measure perversely prints NEGATIVE real yields, which is where my left tail comes from). P90 3.0 (fiscal dominance, Debt-at-Risk realisation, retiree dissaving raising r*, term-premium spike, plus the UK step).","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:51.289Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"TÜİK publishes Türkiye calendar-2029 core CPI (ex food and energy, annual average) below 8.0%, and OECD.Stat's OECD-total core aggregate narrows to within 0.25pp of the G7 core aggregate.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31 2030 (Jan-2030 print plus OECD aggregate revision)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Removes ~0.35pp of the composition floor that carries my CQ2 OECD conjunct and my CQ6-C mass. CQ2 falls from 49 to ~41 (conjunct a from 0.86 to ~0.72); CQ6-C falls ~6pp to ~24 with the mass going to B (~53) and D (~10). CQ4 P50 unchanged.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Eurostat publishes S